   "video-caption": "<p>In the past year, we&rsquo;ve had some pretty big names come perform at the Tiny Desk: <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2019/07/29/732097345/lizzo-tiny-desk-concert\" target=\"_blank\">Lizzo</a>, <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2020/01/29/800256839/jimmy-eat-world-tiny-desk-concert\" target=\"_blank\">Jimmy Eat World</a> and <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2019/10/16/770318649/taylor-swift-tiny-desk-concert\" target=\"_blank\">Taylor Swift</a>, to name a few.</p><p>While seeing these artists&rsquo; stripped-down sets is impressive, that&rsquo;s not all the Tiny Desk is about. For me, what&rsquo;s really magical and memorable about Tiny Desk concerts is discovering and connecting with musicians our audience likely doesn&rsquo;t know and then getting to share them with our listeners.</p><p>We started the Tiny Desk Contest in 2014 in an effort to do even more of that: discover and share great unknown artists. Since the Contest&rsquo;s launch, we&rsquo;ve had <a href=\"http://tinydeskcontest.npr.org/#previous-winner\" target=\"_blank\">five outstanding winners</a>, invited <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLy2PCKGkKRVbn9Rsn99a4VhSGWI4SQrm5\" target=\"_blank\">even more Contest artists</a> to play at the Desk and heard from countless <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/allsongs/2019/05/22/725412654/tiny-desk-top-shelf\" target=\"_blank\">artists we love</a> along the way. We&rsquo;re excited today to announce that the 2020 Tiny Desk Contest is here.</p><p>Here&rsquo;s what you need to know:</p><ul><li>We&rsquo;ll start accepting Contest entries next Tuesday, Feb. 11 at 10 a.m. ET. Entries close at midnight ET on Monday, March 30.</li><li>To be eligible to win, you must be an unsigned musician and at least 18 years old.</li><li>To enter, record a video of yourself playing one original song at a desk (any desk will do!) and upload it to YouTube.</li><li>Send us your song by submitting your video at <a href=\"http://npr.org/tinydeskcontest\" target=\"_blank\">npr.org/tinydeskcontest</a>.</li><li>The winner will be chosen by a panel of judges. I&rsquo;ll be joined by some great Tiny Desk alums: <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2019/10/15/768439696/brittany-howard-tiny-desk-concert\" target=\"_blank\">Brittany Howard</a>, <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2015/09/22/441220834/gina-chavez-tiny-desk-concert\" target=\"_blank\">Gina Chavez</a> and last year&rsquo;s winner, <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2019/06/03/728694436/quinn-christopherson-tiny-desk-concert\" target=\"_blank\">Quinn Christopherson</a>. Bobby Carter, Tiny Desk concert producer extraordinaire, will be part of the team, plus <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/people/774752634/raina-douris\" target=\"_blank\">Raina Douris</a> of <a href=\"https://xpn.org/\" target=\"_blank\">WXPN</a>&rsquo;s World Cafe and <a href=\"https://radiomilwaukee.org/about-us/station-staff/tarik-moody/\" target=\"_blank\">Tarik Moody</a> of <a href=\"https://radiomilwaukee.org/\" target=\"_blank\">88Nine Radio Milwaukee</a>.</li></ul><p>If you want to make sure your video is eligible to win, you can take this <a href=\"https://tinydeskcontest.npr.org/2020/rules-quiz\" target=\"_blank\">easy quiz</a> or read the <a href=\"https://tinydeskcontest.npr.org/rules\" target=\"_blank\">official rules</a>.</p><h2><a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/allsongs/2020/02/04/802281228/the-tiny-desk-contest-is-back-for-2020?utm_source=tumblr.com&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_campaign=npr&amp;utm_term=nprnews&amp;utm_content=20200205\" target=\"_blank\">The Tiny Desk Contest Is Back For 2020</a></h2><p><i>Video: NPR</i></p>",
